# .env.example (REPO ROOT)
#
# Copy this file to .env (in the same directory as docker-compose.yml, NOT inside src/).
# Fill in one token per agent profile before running `docker compose --profile <agent> up -d`.
#
# The .env file is listed in .gitignore (**/.env) and MUST NEVER be committed.
# There is intentionally NO default and NO committed token.
#
# PLACEMENT: this file belongs at the repo root (same directory as docker-compose.yml).
# Compose reads .env from the same directory as the compose file; it does NOT read src/.env.
# src/.env is no longer used by any service (ADR-009 D-B, FIX-F1 2026-06-20).
#
# CREDENTIAL ISOLATION (ADR-008 D3 / ADR-009 D-B):
# Each token is scoped to EXACTLY ONE agent profile by absence-of-declaration.
# A token can reach a container only if that container's environment: block names its key.
# Fill in only the token(s) for the profile(s) you intend to use.
# Do NOT put all three agents' tokens in the same environment at the same time if you can
# avoid it; populate the one you are actively using and leave the others empty.

# ============================================================
# COPILOT PROFILE (docker compose --profile copilot up)
# Declared ONLY in: devcontainer (copilot) service.
# ============================================================
#
# HOW TO MINT:
#   Option A (preferred): Fine-grained PAT with minimum scope
#     github.com -> Settings -> Developer settings -> Personal access tokens
#     -> Fine-grained tokens -> Create with Copilot Requests: Read-only
#     (Resource owner must be your personal account, not an org.)
#     Expiration: shortest acceptable (1 day to 1 week recommended).
#
#   Option B: Extract from a host-side 'copilot login'
#     cat ~/.config/github-copilot/hosts.json   # or apps.json
#     Copy the oauth_token value.
#
# Token starts with github_pat_... (fine-grained) or gho_... (OAuth).
COPILOT_GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ============================================================
# CLAUDE CODE PROFILE (docker compose --profile claude up)
# Declared ONLY in: devcontainer-claude service.
# Set EXACTLY ONE of the two options below (not both).
# ============================================================

# Option 1 (preferred): API key - uses only api.anthropic.com (narrow-host path).
# Mint at: console.anthropic.com -> API Keys -> Create Key
# Use a project key with minimum required scope.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Option 2: OAuth subscription token (Pro/Max plan, host-minted).
# Mint on the HOST (not in the container) via:
#   claude setup-token
# The command prints the token; paste it here.
# After minting, leave ANTHROPIC_API_KEY empty and set this one.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# ============================================================
# CODEX CLI PROFILE (docker compose --profile codex up)
# Declared ONLY in: devcontainer-codex service.
# Set EXACTLY ONE of the two options below (not both).
# ============================================================

# Option 1 (preferred): OpenAI API key - uses only api.openai.com (narrow-host path).
# Mint at: platform.openai.com -> API Keys -> Create new secret key
# Use a project-scoped key if available.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Option 2: Codex-specific env var alias (same API key, alternative name accepted by Codex CLI).
CODEX_API_KEY=

# ============================================================
# NOTES
# ============================================================
#
# WHAT NOT TO DO:
#   - Do NOT commit this file with real tokens. The .gitignore covers **/.env.
#   - Do NOT create or use src/.env for credential injection (ADR-009 D-B).
#     src/.env is no longer read by any compose service.
#   - Do NOT run agent login commands inside the container for the first time
#     without first verifying the token path per the agent's onboarding runbook.
#
# RESIDUAL RISK (R-c, accepted):
#   Tokens are readable by the agent process (same UID; /proc/[pid]/environ accessible).
#   This is irreducible. Containment is the egress boundary, NOT unreadability.
#   See docs/decisions/residual-risk-register.md R-c.
#
# DETECT STACK: src/detect/.env.example covers the immudb admin credential for the
# detection stack (docker compose -f src/detect/docker-compose.detect.yml). It is
# separate from this file and still valid.
